acing to interacting).\n\nHowever, in the **entire 13-frame sequence**, Maury Povich:\n- Is **absent for most of the video** (frames 1–5, 11–13)\n- When present (frames 6–10), he is **only seated and interacting** — **no change in movement pattern** occurs.\n\nThus, **there is no discernible “change” in movement** — he doesn’t transition from one state to another (e.g., standing → sitting, or walking → sitting). He simply appears seated and stays that way.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Correct Interpretation\n\nThe host’s movement **does not change** throughout the video — he is **only seen seated and interacting** when visible, and **absent otherwise**.\n\nTherefore, **answering “2” (sitting)** is **incomplete and misleading** because it ignores the **lack of movement change** and the **temporal absence** of the host.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Final Answer: **No, '2' is not correct.**  \nThe host’s movement does not meaningfully change — he is only seen seated and interacting in a limited segment, with no transition or variation in movement pattern across the video. The question requires evidence of *change*, which is absent."}], 'formatted_responses': ['\n=== Batch 0-30 (29 frames) ===\nFrames: /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/4LA_tH-VSnQ/frames/frame_0001.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/4LA_tH-VSnQ/frames/frame_0002.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/4LA_tH-VSnQ/frames/frame_0003.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/4LA_tH-VSnQ/frames/frame_0004.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/4LA_tH-VSnQ/frames/frame_0005.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/4LA_tH-VSnQ/frames/frame_0006.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/4LA_tH-VSnQ/frames/frame_0802.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/4LA_tH-VSnQ/frames/frame_0803.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/4LA_tH-VSnQ/frames/frame_0804.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/4LA_tH-VSnQ/frames/frame_0805.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/4LA_tH-VSnQ/frames/frame_0806